VeridianOS: gengtype-lex: give trailing-context rules their own action

GCC reported, twice per compile of gengtype-lex.cc (built twice, as
build/gengtype-lex.o and gengtype-lex.o; 4 warnings in all):

  gengtype-lex.cc:356:15: warning: this statement may fall through
    [-Wimplicit-fallthrough=]
  gengtype-lex.l:108:1: note: in expansion of macro 'YY_DO_BEFORE_ACTION'

Two rules in gengtype-lex.l have trailing context (/{EOID}) and share
the next rule's action with '|':

  {CXX_KEYWORD}/{EOID} |  "~" |  "^" |  "&"  { ... IGNORABLE_CXX_KEYWORD }
  {IWORD}({WS}{IWORD})*/{EOID} |  "ENUM_BITFIELD"(...)  { ... SCALAR }

For a trailing-context rule flex emits code that gives the trailing
context back to the input (ending in YY_DO_BEFORE_ACTION) in the rule's
own case; with '|' that code then falls through into the next rule's
case label, which is what GCC flags.  Each of the two rules now has its
own action: the two-line IGNORABLE_CXX_KEYWORD action is repeated, and
the SCALAR action moves into a helper, scalar_token, called by both of
its rules.  Rule order and patterns are unchanged, so every rule matches
what it did before.  The fall-through itself was intended (the shared
action ran on the trimmed yytext); behaviour is unchanged.

gengtype-lex.cc is shipped pre-generated in the release tarball and is
regenerated here with the same flex (2.6.4) and the header that the
gengtype-lex.cc rule in gcc/Makefile.in prepends; flex 2.6.4 on the
unmodified .l reproduces the shipped file byte for byte.  The .l hunk
comes first so that the .cc ends up newer and make does not rerun flex
(if it does, it produces the same file).

Checked: gengtype linked with the old and with the new lexer writes a
byte-identical gtype.state for the whole GCC source tree (gtyp-input.list
of this build).

diff -ru a/gcc/gengtype-lex.l b/gcc/gengtype-lex.l
--- a/gcc/gengtype-lex.l	2026-08-07 03:46:06.193690368 -0400
+++ b/gcc/gengtype-lex.l	2026-10-08 16:58:48.232928305 -0400
@@ -37,6 +37,24 @@
       lexer_line.line++;
 }
 
+/* Set *YYLVAL to the scalar type name TEXT (LEN characters, trailing
+   white space dropped) and return SCALAR.  A function rather than an
+   action shared with '|': a rule with trailing context cannot share its
+   action, since flex's code for the trailing context would then fall
+   through into the next case.  */
+static int
+scalar_token (const char **yylval, const char *text, size_t len)
+{
+  size_t vlen;
+
+  for (vlen = len; ISSPACE (text[vlen-1]); vlen--)
+    ;
+
+  *yylval = XDUPVAR (const char, text, vlen, vlen+1);
+  update_lineno (text, len);
+  return SCALAR;
+}
+
 %}
 
 CID	[[:alpha:]_][[:alnum:]_]*
@@ -98,7 +116,10 @@
 \\\n				{ lexer_line.line++; }
 
 "const"/{EOID}			/* don't care */
-{CXX_KEYWORD}/{EOID}			|
+{CXX_KEYWORD}/{EOID}			{
+    *yylval = XDUPVAR (const char, yytext, yyleng, yyleng + 1);
+    return IGNORABLE_CXX_KEYWORD;
+}
 "~"					|
 "^"					|
 "&"					{
@@ -119,16 +140,11 @@
   return NUM;
 }
 
-{IWORD}({WS}{IWORD})*/{EOID}		|
+{IWORD}({WS}{IWORD})*/{EOID}		{
+  return scalar_token (yylval, yytext, yyleng);
+}
 "ENUM_BITFIELD"{WS}?"("{WS}?{ID}{WS}?")"	{
-  size_t len;
-
-  for (len = yyleng; ISSPACE (yytext[len-1]); len--)
-    ;
-
-  *yylval = XDUPVAR (const char, yytext, len, len+1);
-  update_lineno (yytext, yyleng);
-  return SCALAR;
+  return scalar_token (yylval, yytext, yyleng);
 }
 
 {ID}/{EOID}			{
